title: Lore, opt-in search, declarative mods, and schedules
---
date: 2026-10-18
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: Parity milestones five to seven add retrieval memory, a single fixed search path, validated macros and appearance, and server-side schedules, each defaulting to off.
---
tags: ai, privacy, user-control, architecture
---
source_commit: d28f6a5a2bcbf9d98e7c5e4f91d6be5e2bd62e27
---
body:

The next three milestones added the features most likely to send private text
somewhere, and each was built around a conservative default.

**Memory.** Lore storybooks, append-only summaries, and hybrid retrieval were
added with automatic summaries off and retrieval limited to tags, so nothing
sends old messages to a model unasked. A summary applies only when its anchor is
on the visible branch, so edits and forks never inherit stale ones. Retrieval
records keep ids and scores, not text.

**Search and mods.** Web search has three gates, all enforced on the server: an
owner switch, a stored key, and a per-message request. Its destination is a
constant, not a setting, because a configurable URL could redirect a key and the
user's text anywhere; a test guards the constructor. The query is typed text with
macro tags removed, since a macro could carry private text. Macros are validated
as a set so a loop or growth bomb cannot reach a send. Appearance is an allowlist
applied through the style object model, which keeps the strict content security
policy intact.

**Schedules and profiles.** Unattended runs have a small cap on follow-ups, never
confirm model loading, and record missed times without replaying them. Profiles
bundle settings but share the database, and the interface says they do not
isolate data.

Real embedding, search, and summarizer services were not exercised here.

[Commit d28f6a5](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/d28f6a5a2bcbf9d98e7c5e4f91d6be5e2bd62e27)
